{"type":"message","id":"a4c905f8","parentId":"dcfd2d78","timestamp":"2026-04-07T00:29:55.864Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"web_search_1775521794518_43","toolName":"web_search","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"query\": \"Tunnelblick command line enable VPN\",\n  \"provider\": \"brave\",\n  \"count\": 5,\n  \"tookMs\": 1082,\n  \"externalContent\": {\n    \"untrusted\": true,\n    \"source\": \"web_search\",\n    \"provider\": \"brave\",\n    \"wrapped\": true\n  },\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"c07a0e76e1a2f4e0\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nCommand Line Installation of Tunnelblick and Configurations - Tunnelblick | Free open source OpenVPN VPN client server software GUI for Mac OS X.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"c07a0e76e1a2f4e0\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://tunnelblick.net/cInstallFromCommandLine.html\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"9893b9778a2c45f1\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nCommand Line Installation of Tunnelblick and Configurations - Tunnelblick | Free open source OpenVPN VPN client server software GUI for Mac OS X.. Includes OpenVPN, OpenSSL, easy-rsa, and drivers.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"9893b9778a2c45f1\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"September 11, 2023\",\n      \"siteName\": \"tunnelblick.net\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"0cec1516bd3883d1\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nHow to start Tunnelblick VPN connection via Terminal - Ask Different\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"0cec1516bd3883d1\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://apple.stackexchange.com/questions/198163/how-to-start-tunnelblick-vpn-connection-via-terminal\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"0acca3dd1d61c793\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n@user14492 you mean something like this? github.com/hlissner/lb6-actions/tree/master/VPN.lbaction/… ... A possibly better idea than messing around with openvpn directly (Tunnelblick is basically just a fancy GUI around it) would be to use an Applescript, something that can definitely be launched from the terminal (i.e. with osascript) ... tell application &quot;Tunnelblick&quot; connect &quot;Company_VPN&quot; get state of first configuration where name = &quot;Company_VPN&quot; repeat until result = &quot;CONNECTED&quot; delay 1 get state of first configuration where name = &quot;Company_VPN&quot; end repeat end tell\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"0acca3dd1d61c793\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"apple.stackexchange.com\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"99414424d1ec2eea\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nInstalling and Deleting VPN Configurations - Tunnelblick | Free open source OpenVPN VPN client server software GUI for Mac OS X.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"99414424d1ec2eea\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://tunnelblick.net/cInstallConfigs.html\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"fa11ffc2b831a184\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nInstalling and Deleting VPN Configurations - Tunnelblick | Free open source OpenVPN VPN client server software GUI for Mac OS X.. Includes OpenVPN, OpenSSL, easy-rsa, and drivers.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"fa11ffc2b831a184\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"tunnelblick.net\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"9976e70ac41231bd\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nGitHub - benwebber/tunnelblickctl: :lock: Command-line interface for Tunnelblick\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"9976e70ac41231bd\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/benwebber/tunnelblickctl\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"078c03975a48c102\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nCommand-line interface for Tunnelblick, the de facto OpenVPN client for OS X. brew tap benwebber/tunnelblickctl brew install tunnelblickctl · Download one of the pre-compiled releases, extract it, then copy tunnelblickctl to somewhere on your $PATH. $ tunnelblickctl help tunnelblickctl USAGE: tunnelblickctl [SUBCOMMAND] FLAGS: -h, --help Prints help information SUBCOMMANDS: connect Connect to a VPN disconnect Disconnect from a VPN help Prints this message or the help of the given subcommand(s) install Install an OpenVPN or Tunnelblick configuration launch Launch Tunnelblick list List VPN configurations [aliases: ls] quit Quit Tunnelblick status Show VPN connection status version Show version information\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"078c03975a48c102\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"github.com\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"5f284bca0dd6c18f\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nGitHub - owaism/tunnelblick-cmdline-vpn-connect: Apple Scripts that will enable you to connect to a TunnelBlick VPN using your command line\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"5f284bca0dd6c18f\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/owaism/tunnelblick-cmdline-vpn-connect\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"8514e94ff4bf083b\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nAllows you to open up VPN Connection using your command prompt ... Its easier to create aliases for for each of your VPN Profiles. Something like: alias vpn=&quot;osascript tunnelblick_connect.scpt &lt;VPN-CONFIG-NAME&gt;&quot;\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"8514e94ff4bf083b\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"github.com\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"}],"details":{"query":"Tunnelblick command line enable VPN","provider":"brave","count":5,"tookMs":1082,"externalContent":{"untrusted":true,"source":"web_search","provider":"brave","wrapped":true},"results":[{"title":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"c07a0e76e1a2f4e0\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nCommand Line Installation of Tunnelblick and Configurations - Tunnelblick | Free open source OpenVPN VPN client server software GUI for Mac OS X.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"c07a0e76e1a2f4e0\">>>","url":"https://tunnelblick.net/cInstallFromCommandLine.html","description":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"9893b9778a2c45f1\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nCommand Line Installation of Tunnelblick and Configurations - Tunnelblick | Free open source OpenVPN VPN client server software GUI for Mac OS X.. Includes OpenVPN, OpenSSL, easy-rsa, and drivers.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"9893b9778a2c45f1\">>>","published":"September 11, 2023","siteName":"tunnelblick.net"},{"title":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"0cec1516bd3883d1\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nHow to start Tunnelblick VPN connection via Terminal - Ask Different\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"0cec1516bd3883d1\">>>","url":"https://apple.stackexchange.com/questions/198163/how-to-start-tunnelblick-vpn-connection-via-terminal","description":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"0acca3dd1d61c793\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n@user14492 you mean something like this? github.com/hlissner/lb6-actions/tree/master/VPN.lbaction/… ... A possibly better idea than messing around with openvpn directly (Tunnelblick is basically just a fancy GUI around it) would be to use an Applescript, something that can definitely be launched from the terminal (i.e. with osascript) ... tell application &quot;Tunnelblick&quot; connect &quot;Company_VPN&quot; get state of first configuration where name = &quot;Company_VPN&quot; repeat until result = &quot;CONNECTED&quot; delay 1 get state of first configuration where name = &quot;Company_VPN&quot; end repeat end tell\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"0acca3dd1d61c793\">>>","siteName":"apple.stackexchange.com"},{"title":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"99414424d1ec2eea\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nInstalling and Deleting VPN Configurations - Tunnelblick | Free open source OpenVPN VPN client server software GUI for Mac OS X.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"99414424d1ec2eea\">>>","url":"https://tunnelblick.net/cInstallConfigs.html","description":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"fa11ffc2b831a184\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nInstalling and Deleting VPN Configurations - Tunnelblick | Free open source OpenVPN VPN client server software GUI for Mac OS X.. Includes OpenVPN, OpenSSL, easy-rsa, and drivers.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"fa11ffc2b831a184\">>>","siteName":"tunnelblick.net"},{"title":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"9976e70ac41231bd\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nGitHub - benwebber/tunnelblickctl: :lock: Command-line interface for Tunnelblick\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"9976e70ac41231bd\">>>","url":"https://github.com/benwebber/tunnelblickctl","description":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"078c03975a48c102\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nCommand-line interface for Tunnelblick, the de facto OpenVPN client for OS X. brew tap benwebber/tunnelblickctl brew install tunnelblickctl · Download one of the pre-compiled releases, extract it, then copy tunnelblickctl to somewhere on your $PATH. $ tunnelblickctl help tunnelblickctl USAGE: tunnelblickctl [SUBCOMMAND] FLAGS: -h, --help Prints help information SUBCOMMANDS: connect Connect to a VPN disconnect Disconnect from a VPN help Prints this message or the help of the given subcommand(s) install Install an OpenVPN or Tunnelblick configuration launch Launch Tunnelblick list List VPN configurations [aliases: ls] quit Quit Tunnelblick status Show VPN connection status version Show version information\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"078c03975a48c102\">>>","siteName":"github.com"},{"title":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"5f284bca0dd6c18f\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nGitHub - owaism/tunnelblick-cmdline-vpn-connect: Apple Scripts that will enable you to connect to a TunnelBlick VPN using your command line\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"5f284bca0dd6c18f\">>>","url":"https://github.com/owaism/tunnelblick-cmdline-vpn-connect","description":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"8514e94ff4bf083b\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nAllows you to open up VPN Connection using your command prompt ... Its easier to create aliases for for each of your VPN Profiles. Something like: alias vpn=&quot;osascript tunnelblick_connect.scpt &lt;VPN-CONFIG-NAME&gt;&quot;\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"8514e94ff4bf083b\">>>","siteName":"github.com"}]},"isError":false,"timestamp":1775521795738}}
{"type":"message","id":"d42f3a28","parentId":"a4c905f8","timestamp":"2026-04-07T00:29:59.345Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Para ligar o Tunnelblick, posso usar um AppleScript. No entanto, preciso do **nome exato da sua conexão VPN** configurada no Tunnelblick (por exemplo, \"Minha_VPN_do_Trabalho\").\n\nPode me informar qual é o nome da configuração que você deseja ligar?","textSignature":""}],"api":"google-generative-ai","provider":"google","model":"gemini-2.5-flash","usage":{"input":166539,"output":248,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":166787,"cost":{"input":0.0499617,"output":0.00062,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0505817}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1775521795865,"responseId":"BFDUadWSMNrTz7IPjO3Y0QM"}}
